<title>CHINA: China retains tariff holidays on zinc, tin, lead.</title>
<headline>China retains tariff holidays on zinc, tin, lead.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>China announced on Friday that exports of lead, zinc and tin would continue to be subject to a temporary preferential tariff system next year.  </p>
<p>The tariff commission under the State Council, or cabinet, had decided to scrap export tariffs on 14 items, including cashmere, raw silk and silk, from January 1, state television said.</p>
<p>The items include chestnuts, pigment, methylbenzene, silk cocoons, raw silk, silk yarn, various silk products, cashmere, uncast lead and scrap lead, it said.</p>
<p>China would retain tariffs on 35 items, including eel fry, it said but gave no more details.</p>
</text>
